WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:04.400
June 2014.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.710
Flying over remote Utah desert.

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:10.130
Eyes in the sky Capture this image.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:12.880
This is crazy.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.840
In the middle of what looks to be nowhere.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.860
There's a very purposeful pattern.

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:28.430
Further images reveal yet more unusual shapes
in the desert.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:29.600
Scrub below.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.120
These patterns come in different shapes and
sizes.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.820
There's one that looks like a big ice cube
tray.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.520
One kind of looks like a wagon wheel.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:43.830
So what possible purpose could be served by
creating these patterns on the desert in

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:45.510
close proximity to one another?

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:53.510
Analysts consider if the shapes are a legacy
of the indigenous tribes who once ruled these

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:54.260
lands.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.930
This area was inhabited by tribes of the
Navajo Nation, and they use numerous symbols

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:00.800
in their culture.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:06.170
Elsewhere, giant symbols have been found
carved into the earth.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:12.950
Some are believed to have had a magical
function, possibly a form of prayer or an

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:16.160
attempt to communicate with gods who inhabit
the skies.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.350
Some of these symbols were for protection,
some of them were for life giving and some

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:25.610
were for luck. So I'm wondering, maybe the
things we're seeing here could be Native

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:26.810
American symbols.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:35.610
Yet studies of Utah's Indigenous people
suggest the strange patterns aren't some kind

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:36.900
of ancient code.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:43.940
It's unlikely because they usually put their
symbols into rock faces, not on the ground.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:58.380
Military journalist Carlo Munoz suspects the
patterns may have a sinister purpose and is

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.780
traveling to the remote site to investigate.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:02.940
We're we're driving right now.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:08.130
We're near one of the US government's most
important sort of training grounds for

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:09.810
chemical and biological weapons.

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:17.360
Munoz knows that experimental military
testing takes many forms and can leave long

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.360
lasting scars on the landscape.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:21.800
There's got to be some sort of connection.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:24.590
I just can't put my finger on exactly what
that could be.

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:29.990
One notorious Utah base could help shed some
light.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:35.350
It's entirely possible that these symbols are
connected to the Dugway Proving Ground.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:39.280
The operations that go on at Dugway are
really top secret.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:40.480
I mean, these.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:45.890
Are the types of operations that you would
put maybe on par with something going on at

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.000
Area 51.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:54.500
Declassified records confirm Dugway
scientists have been conducting clandestine

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:59.030
bioweapons experiments in the Utah desert
for almost 80 years.

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:07.360
These include trialling the aerial dispersal
of gas, weaponized mosquitoes and fleas

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:09.340
infected with the bubonic plague.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:17.840
Dugway aerial experiments here remains some
of the most controversial in US military

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:18.530
history.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:21.780
With the high level of activity at Dugway
Proving Ground.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:25.220
It's quite possible that these shapes are
related to what's going on there.

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:30.110
Could they be targets? Could they be some
sort of side effect?

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:32.390
Some of these tests, I don't know what.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:33.710
We're going to go see what's happening.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.770
The desert road stops long before the shapes
begin.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:46.650
All right. This looks about as far as I'm
able to go.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:03.410
Munoz approaches the location indicated by
the aerial images.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:05.390
But finding them isn't easy.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:09.860
You know, you look at the satellite image,
the symbol just pops out.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.130
But here on the ground.

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:17.530
I mean, seeing what I'm seeing, I could be
standing right on top of it, not even know.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.630
Okay, You know what?

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:40.650
I think this is it.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:47.430
You've got two paths going this way.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:49.240
You turn here.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.180
You have the same exact sort of pattern.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:54.450
Here. Turn again and it's there again.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.090
So this this is probably the center of it.

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:02.910
From the ground. The symbol lacks the
precision visible from the air.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:08.220
Whatever this is, Munoz doesn't think
military testing can explain it.

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:12.880
I'm not seeing any signs of military
activity.

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:15.070
There's no craters or whatnot.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:20.620
So this is clearly not some kind of
extension of a military base.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.270
The desert floor yields some clues.

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:30.330
This is all loose sand as long as I've been
walking.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:35.640
But coming down here, looking down this
path.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:37.860
This is packed down.

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:41.520
This is almost designed to take a very heavy
weight.

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:50.170
The shape is huge, Munoz reckons.

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:52.120
12,000 square feet.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:55.830
The plant growth suggests it may be decades
old.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.570
Whoever built this thing, they built it to
last.

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:03.140
Why would someone do that?

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:09.590
What makes it even weirder is we know that
there are several other symbols out here just

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:10.220
as big.

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:18.190
Munoz thinks the shapes nearby must be
connected.

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:22.810
That symbol may have been similar to
something like.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:25.140
The X on a treasure map.

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:27.590
Well, the question is.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.040
What exactly were they looking for?

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:34.090
Munoz turns to aerial images for help.

00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:39.770
To the north. He spots what could be a small
abandoned mine.

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:46.340
If I can figure out what exactly they were
mining out of this old mine, hopefully I can

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:48.380
figure out what these symbols out here for.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.130
Munoz sets out further into Utah's perilous
desert.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:07.210
It was not until the late 18th century that
Europeans dared to explore these arid lands.

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:12.370
There it is.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:25.260
Beyond the mining huts, Munoz spots an
entrance into the rock face.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:33.250
Oh, wow. Oh.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:35.820
So this is the mine.

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:38.610
What? It looks like we're a little barred
off here.

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:40.080
It's not going to be able to get in.

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:44.220
This can't be a gold mine.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:49.100
The nearest known deposits of gold lie far
to the north and east of here.

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:58.240
If you take a look, look how far that goes
into the rock face.

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:04.210
I've heard of mines like this kind of carved
right into rock.

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:06.910
And it could be a uranium mine.

